 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N_{tiles})$ for the output `ranges` array [G].
-*   **Performance:** This kernel is extremely lightweight and typically completes in negligible time compared to the sorting and rasterization phases. It is memory-bandwidth bound due to reading `point_list_keys` and writing `ranges`, but the working set is small [G].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple parallel logic, no synchronization barriers required between threads, minimal overhead [G].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires the list to be fully sorted by tile ID before execution. Does not handle unsorted input [G].
